// The modules of this repository, so that a build from a checkout uses the
// working tree rather than whatever version each of them last recorded.
//
// It is committed, and that is the point. The binary imports the sinks and the
// sinks import the root, which is a cycle between modules -- legal, and quiet
// as long as nothing has to resolve the recorded versions. This is what stops
// anything having to. The CI job that builds each module with GOWORK=off is
// what says when one of them has fallen behind.
go 1.26.4

use (
	.
	./sink/s3
)
